Hi all
It turns out that I had specified the 1st heirarchy of some keyword names with a space, and of course R does not like this when constructing column titles for dataframes (if only I had paid more attention to vignette 1!). After renaming my keyword titles (in digiKam) from for example 'ID confidence score' to 'IDConfidencescore' the metadata extraction is now working well. The code I am using is as follows.

rec.db.species_metadata <- recordTable(inDir = raw_images, IDfrom = "metadata", cameraID = "directory", camerasIndependent = TRUE,

                              metadataSpeciesTag = "Species", metadataHierarchyDelimitor = "|", minDeltaTime = 0,

                              timeZone = "Australia/Tasmania", removeDuplicateRecords = FALSE,

                              returnFileNamesMissingTags = TRUE, writecsv = FALSE,

                              additionalMetadataTags = c("EXIF:Model", "EXIF:Make", "metadata_IDConfidenceScore","metadata_Group","metadata_CameraMalfunction"))

